# CODEOWNERS: ADR-028 autonomy charter (control plane). Supersedes the ADR-023 Phase-2 split.
#
# Two review authorities, by blast radius:
#   * ORG-GOVERNED (everything outside the safety kernel): standards/**, loops/**,
#     registry/**, ADRs, agents/employees|templates/**, charter/PRD.md and GLOSSARY.md,
#     work/**, product/**, roadmap/**, docs/**, and ledger entries. Reviewed by the
#     machine account @scope-creep-review. GitHub blocks it from approving its own PRs,
#     so author != merger holds (INVARIANTS §10).
#   * SAFETY KERNEL (INVARIANTS v2.0.0 §4): reviewed by the HUMAN Owner @dimays ONLY.
#     The unattended reviewer is deliberately NOT a code owner here, so the org can
#     never approve and merge a change to its own gates.
#
# Keep this list in lockstep with scripts/escalation-check.sh is_escalation().
# The last matching pattern wins, so the kernel is listed AFTER the default.
# Exact paths are used for the executive charters (not /agents/*.md). The
# routine-reviewer matches these patterns with bash `case`, where * also matches '/',
# so a glob would wrongly hold agents/templates/ and agents/employees/.

# --- org-governed default: routine review by the machine account ---
*                                       @scope-creep-review

# --- safety kernel: HUMAN-ONLY Owner review (@dimays) ---
# (a) the Owner-held charter docs and the instructions every agent loads
/charter/INVARIANTS.md                  @dimays
/charter/PRINCIPLES.md                  @dimays
/AGENTS.md                              @dimays
# (b) gate-enforcement surface
/.claude/                               @dimays
/.github/workflows/                     @dimays
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @dimays
/scripts/escalation-check*.sh           @dimays
/scripts/guard-*.sh                     @dimays
/scripts/routine-reviewer*              @dimays
/scripts/owner-runbook/                 @dimays
/docs/owner-apply-routine-reviewer.md   @dimays
# (c) the escalation model
/standards/decision-rights.md           @dimays
# (d) executive and standing-function charters (exact files; employees/templates are org-governed)
/agents/ceo.md                          @dimays
/agents/chief-of-staff.md               @dimays
/agents/cto.md                          @dimays
/agents/chief-designer.md               @dimays
/agents/chief-knowledge-manager.md      @dimays
/agents/chief-product-officer.md        @dimays
/agents/chief-reality-officer.md        @dimays
/agents/code-reviewer.md                @dimays
/agents/git-manager.md                  @dimays
/agents/qa-tester.md                    @dimays
# (e) dependency and infra manifests, anywhere in the tree (supply chain)
package.json                            @dimays
package-lock.json                       @dimays
npm-shrinkwrap.json                     @dimays
yarn.lock                               @dimays
pnpm-lock.yaml                          @dimays
bun.lock                                @dimays
bun.lockb                               @dimays
Dockerfile                              @dimays
fly.toml                                @dimays
Procfile                                @dimays
*.tf                                    @dimays
*.tfvars                                @dimays
# ledger POLICY only; append entries stay org-governed
/ledger/README.md                       @dimays
